Found while closing karr #4 (shipping resource.k8s.io v1beta1/v1beta2).

%DEFAULT_RESOURCE_MAP in lib/IO/K8s.pm maps each short Kind name (DeviceClass,
ResourceClaim, ResourceClaimTemplate, ResourceSlice, ...) to exactly ONE class
path -- currently always the V1 (GA) version. expand_class() accepts an
api_version parameter for disambiguation (used by inflate(), which passes
struct->{apiVersion}), but only domain-qualified map entries
("$api_version/$kind") are consulted for that, and those are only ever
populated by add() when merging an EXTERNAL provider that collides with an
existing short name. The built-in %DEFAULT_RESOURCE_MAP itself never gets
domain-qualified keys.

Consequence, reproduced against DeviceClass:

  IO::K8s->new->inflate({
    apiVersion => "resource.k8s.io/v1beta1",
    kind       => "DeviceClass",
    metadata   => { name => "x" },
    spec       => { selectors => [] },
  });
  # silently returns a IO::K8s::Api::Resource::V1::DeviceClass instance,
  # NOT V1beta1::DeviceClass -- wrong schema version, no error.

And for a Kind never added to the short-name map at all (DeviceTaintRule,
ResourcePoolStatusRequest -- both already shipped, v1beta2/v1alpha3
respectively):

  IO::K8s->new->inflate({ apiVersion => "resource.k8s.io/v1beta2",
    kind => "DeviceTaintRule", ... });
  # dies: Cant locate IO/K8s/DeviceTaintRule.pm in @INC
  # (falls through to the bare IO::K8s::$kind fallback, which does not exist)

This is pre-existing and not introduced by karr #4 -- it already affected the
already-shipped V1alpha3 "classic DRA" DeviceClass/ResourceClaim/etc. and the
V1beta2 DeviceTaintRule family the same way. karr #4 only adds more classes
that hit the identical gap (v1beta1 DeviceClass/ResourceClaim/
ResourceClaimTemplate/ResourceSlice, v1beta2 same four). Today the only
reliable way to get a specific non-GA version is to reference the fully
qualified class directly (IO::K8s::Api::Resource::V1beta1::DeviceClass->new
or ->struct_to_object with the full class name), bypassing inflate()s
apiVersion-based dispatch entirely.

Two independent fixes worth considering separately:
  1. Populate domain-qualified keys for every entry in %DEFAULT_RESOURCE_MAP
     itself (not just via add()), so inflate() disambiguates GA vs beta/alpha
     versions of the same Kind correctly.
  2. Add the short-name-less Kinds (DeviceTaintRule, ResourcePoolStatusRequest,
     and now the new v1beta1/v1beta2 quartets) to the map under
     domain-qualified keys at minimum, so inflate() does not die outright.

Repro path: grep expand_class in lib/IO/K8s.pm (~line 232) and
%DEFAULT_RESOURCE_MAP (~line 17).
## Decision: Approach 1 (extend default map with domain-qualified keys)

Picked Approach 1 because:
- Approach 2 alone leaves the GA-vs-beta mis-dispatch bug unfixed
  (DeviceClass v1beta1 silently returns V1::DeviceClass). Approach 1
  fixes both bugs at once.
- Same logic that add() already runs on collision can be reused on
  every default-map entry, so the default and external maps become
  symmetric. add() currently only registers the qualified key for the
  LOSING entry in a collision; with Approach 1, every default entry
  gets a qualified key at instance build time regardless.

Implementation sketch:
- Extract the collision-time 'compute qualified key' logic from add()
  into a helper (e.g. _qualify_default_entry).
- Run it in BUILD over %DEFAULT_RESOURCE_MAP entries.
- expand_class() needs no changes: the new '/' keys
  feed the same code path it already handles for external merges.

Decision logged before coding per house rule 'Surface conflicts, don't
average them'. See _expand_class / BUILD changes in commit.
## Implementation plan (concrete)

1. Extract _qualify_class_path helper in IO::K8s.pm from the existing
   inline logic in add() that, given (map, kind, class_path), adds the
   domain-qualified key '/' to map if the class can
   be loaded and reports an api_version.

2. In BUILD, walk %DEFAULT_RESOURCE_MAP and run the helper for every
   entry, populating qualified keys at instance build time.

3. Refactor add() to call the same helper (no behavior change, just
   dedup).

4. Add qualified-only entries to %DEFAULT_RESOURCE_MAP for the
   short-name-less kinds (DeviceTaintRule, ResourcePoolStatusRequest,
   plus any future short-name-less Kinds under resource.k8s.io that
   ship qualified only).

5. t/40_karr_11_multi_version_dispatch.t added BEFORE the fix as a
   failing regression test, covering:
   - 4 dispatch tests (V1/V1beta1/V1beta2/V1alpha3 DeviceClass)
   - 12 dispatch tests (ResourceClaim/Template/Slice across 3 versions)
   - 2 short-name-less kind tests (DeviceTaintRule, ResourcePoolStatusRequest)
   - 2 domain-qualified expansion tests
   - 2 inflate tests with assertion 'not silently V1'
   - 2 inflate tests for short-name-less Kinds (used to die)
   - 1 round-trip preservation test
   - 2 negative/sanity tests
   - 1 isolation test

